WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.509
Pennywise is back to start a new cycle of
horror that brings the Losers home in an effort

00:00:05.509 --> 00:00:06.810
to defeat IT for good.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:11.270
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video we're diving deep below Derry to

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:15.580
discuss the ending of IT Chapter Two, the
fate of the Losers and the evil clown, and

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:20.109
the secret Maturin turtle easter egg in the
Ritual of Chud that everyone missed!

00:00:20.109 --> 00:00:23.130
Keep watching for details about a special
Pennywise giveaway!

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.429
And, of course, spoilers ahead!

00:00:25.429 --> 00:00:30.779
When the young Losers defeated Pennywise at
the end of the first movie, IT went into hibernation

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:34.650
underground; however, its influence over Derry
remained strong.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:40.800
27 years later, Derry feels "a lot more hopeless,
as if [the town's] making its last dying gasp

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:45.670
before fully succumbing to IT," says screenwriter
Gary Dauberman, and this is brutally evident

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:50.690
early on when a group of thugs beat up Adrian
Mellon in a vicious hate crime, throwing him

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:51.710
into the river.

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:56.000
This signals the return of Pennywise who feeds
on the injured Adrian.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.110
Scrawling bloody messages has always been
part of IT's MO, but now the killer clown

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:05.210
no longer does that to scare away the Losers,
instead he uses gory missives to get them

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:06.469
to return home.

00:01:06.469 --> 00:01:10.950
After waiting and planning vengeance, Pennywise
is desperate to do away with the Losers for

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:15.909
good and pay them back for foiling IT's plans
during the previous cycle, leaving IT hungry.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:17.590
"Now you're the one who's afraid.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:18.950
Because you're gonna starve."

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:24.569
Over time, IT has become more cunning, more
sophisticated in manipulation, and therefore

00:01:24.569 --> 00:01:28.310
deadlier, as we see in Chapter Two during
the scene with young Victoria, which director

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:32.009
Andy Muschietti views as a "mirror scene of
what happened with Georgie".

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:34.829
"Why are you crying?"

00:01:34.829 --> 00:01:39.249
"No one wants to play with me anymore.

00:01:39.249 --> 00:01:42.920
Play a game with me, would ya?

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:45.549
On the count of three.

00:01:45.549 --> 00:01:46.549
One..

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:47.549
Two.."

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:51.920
For actor Bill Skarsgard, present-day Pennywise
has "a strange bond" with the Losers because

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.139
although "he instils fear in humans, [...] he'd
never understood what that was until the Losers,

00:01:57.139 --> 00:01:58.969
and then he felt it for himself."

00:01:58.969 --> 00:02:03.070
Because most of the Losers left town, they
gradually forgot the events they went through

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:04.070
in Derry.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:08.100
But despite their geographical distance from
IT and the fact they've repressed many of

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:13.510
the terrors they endured as children including
the abuse, bullying, bigotry, death of a sibling,

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:18.909
and endless insecurities, their past still
casts a heavy shadow over their present.

00:02:18.909 --> 00:02:22.870
Bill can't find closure in his writing or
real happiness with the wife who isn't the

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:24.129
woman he wants her to be.

00:02:24.129 --> 00:02:27.570
Bev's gone from living with an abusive father
to an abusive husband.

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:31.819
And Eddie hasn't been able to throw off the
shackles of an overbearing parent and is married

00:02:31.819 --> 00:02:34.730
to Myra, a woman who is much like his mother.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:39.700
And fun fact, Eddie's wife Myra is played
by the same actress Molly Atkinson who played

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:41.549
his mother in the first movie.

00:02:41.549 --> 00:02:45.849
The wounds left by IT may not be as fresh
as they were 27 years ago, but the trauma

00:02:45.849 --> 00:02:50.660
the young Losers experienced then still marks
their everyday lives in unconscious ways and

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:55.319
is brought painfully to the surface when they
get a call from Mike, the only one who stayed

00:02:55.319 --> 00:02:58.110
in town and never forgot Pennywise.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:02.409
Each member of the childhood club suffers
a traumatic reaction to Mike's call, with

00:03:02.409 --> 00:03:07.160
Bill suddenly feeling pain in his hand from
the blood oath he made with the others as

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.160
a child.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.319
Out of those who left, Stan has the most harrowing
reaction.

00:03:11.319 --> 00:03:15.460
And I'll discuss that together with his letter
to the others later in the video.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:20.350
The Losers' Chinese restaurant reunion brings
memories of Pennywise flooding back and their

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:24.300
freaky fortune cookie hallucinations cause
a rift in the group.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:28.700
Mike, however, manages to persuade Bill to
go back to the library where he reveals he's

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:33.569
been investigating the history of Pennywise
and how IT came to Derry in the first place.

00:03:33.569 --> 00:03:37.870
Mike shows Bill an 18th-century Native American
artefact that belonged to a group of holy

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:42.330
men that lived outside Derry and who were
beyond the range of IT's influence.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:47.430
Mike secretly spikes Bill's water with a root
that allows him to see a vision of IT's arrival

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:52.269
on Earth via a meteor that crashed underground
in the spot where Derry was later built.

00:03:52.269 --> 00:03:57.159
Bill sees IT's original form, the deadlights,
emerge from the cave and float up to the surface

00:03:57.159 --> 00:04:02.260
where they reform into a bird, then shapeshift
into various monstrous creatures with mouths

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:05.049
full of teeth that devour the people in its
path.

00:04:05.049 --> 00:04:09.599
A crucial detail that Mike also learns from
the Native Americans is a rule that "all living

00:04:09.599 --> 00:04:13.159
things must abide by the laws of the shape
they inhabit."

00:04:13.159 --> 00:04:17.390
This will be critical later for the final
showdown as it means IT can be killed for

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:21.150
good if it transforms into something weak
and vulnerable enough.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:25.710
There's also a very cool easter egg in this
scene which is a twist on the cosmic turtle

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:30.250
from Stephen King's original novel when Mike
calls the root the native American tribe gave

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:32.310
him "their sacred Maturin".

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:36.780
It's an interesting detail that's very hard
to catch as Mike says the name very quickly

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:41.030
and the mention of Maturin's name seems to
indicate that the cosmic turtle is trying

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:44.330
to help the Losers by revealing IT's weaknesses.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:47.220
There's a few other turtle easter eggs in
the first movie.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:53.000
And in Chapter Two, a turtle also shows up
on a desk when Ben revisits an old classroom.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.740
And when the camera turns in that scene, it
looks as if a globe of the Earth is sitting

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:58.280
on the turtle's back.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:03.120
Which is pretty appropriate because for those
who don't know, Maturin is a benevolent interdimensional

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:07.990
entity from King's Macroverse that created
the universe by vomiting it up.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:12.699
The scene also introduces us to the Ritual
of Chud which the original natives of the

00:05:12.699 --> 00:05:16.580
area learned as a technique to attempt to
contain, even destroy IT.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:22.000
We see them standing around a four-sided pyramid
container which works to trap the deadlights.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:26.500
That container is the artefact that Mike has
in his possession, and he explains to the

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:31.080
Losers that the ritual requires they each
sacrifice a token from their childhoods and

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:32.730
burn it in the container.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:37.699
To collect their tokens each Loser spends
the day reliving old memories and confronting

00:05:37.699 --> 00:05:38.699
past horrors.

00:05:38.699 --> 00:05:42.800
For Bev, this means returning to her childhood
home where she retrieves the postcard with

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.419
the poem Ben sent her.

00:05:44.419 --> 00:05:47.889
"Your hair is winter fire, January embers.

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:50.370
My heart burns there, too."

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:55.900
And she also encounters Mrs Kersh transforming
into a giant, grotesque witch and an apparition

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:58.590
of a man turning into Pennywise.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:02.710
Bill recovers the paper boat from the drain
where his little brother was taken as a child

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:06.960
and is reminded of the guilt he's been hiding
about the day Georgie died.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:11.410
Richie's token is a coin from the arcade where
he used to play games as a kid and where,

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:15.440
in a flashback, we discover he was bullied
by Henry Bowers and his cousin who called

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:16.660
him gay.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:21.050
Richie ends up back in the park by the Paul
Bunyan statue which Pennywise brings to life

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:25.099
to attack him while he taunts him about hiding
his sexuality.

00:06:25.099 --> 00:06:27.270
Eddie's token is his inhaler which he picks
up from Mr Keene's drug store where he meets

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:30.759
the creepy old pharmacist again and a now
grown-up Greta.

00:06:30.759 --> 00:06:34.580
He also has a horrifying encounter [in the
basement] with a Leper monster like the one

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:38.830
that attacked him as a child outside the Neibolt
house in the first movie.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:43.730
Ben's token is the yearbook page that Bev
signed for him in Chapter One, and Mike's

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:47.330
is the rock that Bev threw at Henry Bowers
to save him from the bully.

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:51.990
The Losers also include Stan in the ritual
by adding one of the shower caps he bought

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:56.460
for the young Losers to use in their clubhouse
in order to keep their hair free of spiders,

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:59.960
which feels like foreshadowing of their climactic
battle with IT.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:04.789
The Losers then commence the main part of
the ritual by burning the tokens and chanting

00:07:04.789 --> 00:07:07.550
the phrase "turn light into dark".

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:11.940
This summons the deadlights into the artefact;
however, the container immediately swells

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:17.129
up with a huge red balloon which fills the
space until it bursts, revealing Pennywise.

00:07:17.129 --> 00:07:21.330
The clown taunts them that their silly ritual
will never work as when the Native Americans

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.659
tried it they all died.

00:07:23.659 --> 00:07:27.330
Pennywise then reveals that Mike knew that
all along and hid the truth from the others

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:31.729
by scratching out the artefact's drawing of
the deadlights killing the tribe.

00:07:31.729 --> 00:07:35.440
Mike explains the mistake the Native Americans
made was that they didn't believe they could

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:40.190
defeat IT, but Pennywise starts attacking
the Losers, and once again they're split up

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:44.729
and sent off to endure a psychic battle of
wills with IT who confronts each one with

00:07:44.729 --> 00:07:46.840
some of their personal fears.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:51.050
Beverly is thrown back into the school bathroom
stall where, as a child, she was bullied by

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:54.830
Greta and other girls who poured watery trash
all over her.

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:59.300
This time, the stall fills with blood evoking
the blood-soaked bathroom scene from the first

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:00.300
movie.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:05.210
As the stall fills, Bev is tormented by various
abusers banging on the door including her

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:10.699
violent husband, her abusive father, the sleazy
Mr Keene, and her childhood bullies.

00:08:10.699 --> 00:08:15.720
And Henry Bowers even shows up for a quick
"Here's Johnny!" easter egg from The Shining.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:20.439
In the meantime, Ben has been flung into the
underground clubhouse he built as a child.

00:08:20.439 --> 00:08:25.560
As it fills with dirt, Pennywise traps him
inside and taunts him that he'll die alone.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:29.960
This is torture for Ben because, as we learn
early on in Chapter Two, he's been something

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:35.360
of a loner since his Loser days and he's extremely
claustrophobic, living alone in a house full

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:39.599
of floor-to-ceiling windows so he can always
see plenty of space around him.

00:08:39.599 --> 00:08:45.110
In that scene, we also saw the adult Ben advising
his firm's clients to stop putting more walls

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:48.010
into a new retail building that they were
designing.

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:52.579
When we cut back to Beverly, she's almost
drowning in blood and being tormented by her

00:08:52.579 --> 00:08:55.950
father yelling and asking if she's still his
little girl.

00:08:55.950 --> 00:09:00.899
Bev eventually overcomes the shackles of guilt
and shame her father imposed her, and kicks

00:09:00.899 --> 00:09:06.260
the door in his face, finally rejecting him
and the violence against her that he represented.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:10.320
When Ben calls out that he loves her, they're
both able to break through their illusory

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.500
prisons and reach out to each other.

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:16.910
This time, it's Bev who pulls Ben out from
the dirt which is swallowing him up, and saves

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:21.330
him in a reversal of the first movie where
he pulled her out of the Deadlights trance.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:26.110
For Bill, his test is to face a vision of
his dead brother Georgie in the flooded basement

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:27.240
of his childhood home.

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:32.670
At this point, Georgie reveals that Bill wasn't
really sick and blames his older brother for

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:33.690
his fate.

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:36.250
"You lied and I died!

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:38.820
You lied and I died!"

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:43.730
Bill manages to overcome the guilt and blame
that Pennywise is trying to project onto him.

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:48.050
And he shoots the younger version of himself
in the head with a cattle bolt-gun, in a call-back

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:52.529
to how he shot Pennywise masquerading as Georgie
in the first movie.

00:09:52.529 --> 00:09:56.910
The other Losers' personal tests aren't as
intense, with Eddie and Richie going up against

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.390
the "scary" doors.

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:03.310
Richie opens the "Very Scary" door only to
find Betty Ripsom's mutilated legs running

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:08.240
up to him, which harks back to the first movie
when he discovered Betty's shoe in the sewer

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:13.160
and it's also a nod to the "Not Scary At All"
door that Richie opened with Bill in the Neibolt

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:17.620
House where they found the upper half of Betty
Ripsom's mutilated body.

00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:21.310
"Where's my shoe?"

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:26.690
Behind Eddie's door is a cute Pomeranian dog
which turns into a huge monster, an easter

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:29.680
egg to the dog transformation scene from The
Thing.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:34.279
As for Mike, he doesn't seem to have a personal
test, or it might have been cut for time from

00:10:34.279 --> 00:10:35.440
the final movie.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:40.350
After these various battles of wills, the
Losers then go up against IT who has turned

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:45.279
into a horrific Lovecraftian-type Pennywise-spider
or crab hybrid.

00:10:45.279 --> 00:10:49.150
Richie runs up to the monster, but it traps
him in the deadlights, just like Pennywise

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:51.680
did with young Beverly in the first movie.

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:55.660
Eddie sees Richie trapped, and summons up
the courage he previously couldn't muster

00:10:55.660 --> 00:11:01.459
when Richie was being attacked by the Stan-spider
monster, which is another easter egg to The

00:11:01.459 --> 00:11:02.459
Thing.

00:11:02.459 --> 00:11:06.170
Now Eddie takes a metal railing spike that
Beverly gives him and which she also used

00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:10.000
to attack Pennywise in Chapter One, and he
remembers what she told him:

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.220
"Take it, it kills monsters.

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:12.440
If you believe it does."

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:17.300
Eddie finally overcomes his fear and self-doubt,
throwing the spear into IT's mouth [and deadlights],

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:21.880
causing the giant spider-clown to fall back
on the huge spikes in the cavern, severely

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:23.480
injuring the creature.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:28.220
It's heart-breaking when Eddie believes he's
finally triumphed over the monster only for

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:31.820
IT to stab him through the chest, mortally
wounding him.

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:36.529
Before he dies though, Eddie tells the Losers
how he almost killed the leper in the pharmacy

00:11:36.529 --> 00:11:40.790
basement; how when he choked it, he made the
monster small and feel so weak.

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:45.290
The other Losers then realise their only hope
of killing the giant Pennywise-spider is to

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:48.110
make it much smaller and therefore weaker.

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:51.860
With this, the Losers make their final stand
against Pennywise.

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:56.530
Like real-life bullies, many of Pennywise's
tactics employ fear, intimidation, and isolation

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:58.399
to make its victims feel weak.

00:11:58.399 --> 00:12:03.720
So the Losers turn the tables on IT, calling
it names: a stupid clown, a headless boy,

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:07.550
an imposter, a mimic, a bully, a stupid mummy,
and so on.

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:12.220
As they do this, the Losers imprint their
will on the monster and shrink IT down into

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:14.600
a tiny baby-sized clown.

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:19.430
Although IT is an alien form, it has to abide
by the rules of the shapes it inhabits, and

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:24.709
with Pennywise now weak and decrepit, Mike
reaches down and pulls out IT's beating heart.

00:12:24.709 --> 00:12:28.730
Then together the Losers crush it, killing
the evil entity for good.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:33.209
This moment shows that with mental strength,
courage and unity, the Losers could go up

00:12:33.209 --> 00:12:37.600
against the evil that IT represents and defeat
it once and for all.

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:42.980
IT's death brings about the collapse of Pennywise's
lair as the evil beast's power fades away,

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:47.550
and the Losers escape just as the whole of
Neibolt House falls into the sinkhole below,

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:52.640
in a nod to how in King's novel, most of Derry
itself was destroyed after IT was killed.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:57.120
After the trauma of the battle with IT and
Eddie's death, we get a bittersweet throw-back

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:01.990
to the first movie when the five surviving
Losers return to the quarry and Beverly jumps

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:05.840
into the water followed by the remaining four
members of the club.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:10.480
This sad moment where we feel the loss of
both Eddie and Stanley was actually foreshadowed

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:15.050
back in the first film where you can see a
very similar shot of Bev, Bill, Ben, Mike

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:20.190
and Richie together in the water while Eddie
and Stanley are separated from the main group.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:24.730
Next in the film, we see the consequences
of defeating IT for good are even more far-reaching

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:26.820
than the Losers might have imagined.

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:30.980
As they walk into town, Bev discovers that
the deep scar on the palm of her hand from

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:35.779
the blood oath they took as children has completely
disappeared, as also happens in the book.

00:13:35.779 --> 00:13:40.610
Her recurring nightmares of them all dying
if they left town before facing up to Pennywise

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:44.930
are now at an end, and she's proven the killer
clown wrong in his taunts that her actions

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:46.800
haven't changed anything.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:50.769
The disappearing scars fit in nicely with
what producer Barbara Muschietti has said

00:13:50.769 --> 00:13:54.529
about the film's message, that the [pain of
the] past is "a scar that becomes leather

00:13:54.529 --> 00:13:56.860
[…]
At some point, you have to face it.

00:13:56.860 --> 00:14:00.199
You won't be able to finish your life if you
don't get rid of that trauma.

00:14:00.199 --> 00:14:03.470
[The Losers] get courage through unity.

00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:05.139
Pennywise is a master of division.

00:14:05.139 --> 00:14:07.639
He basically wants to divide and conquer.

00:14:07.639 --> 00:14:12.260
Their victory stems from remembering who they
were as kids, and what they were able to do

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:14.470
when the scar was fresh."

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:18.490
Mike also discovers later when he's looking
back at old newspaper cuttings that reported

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:22.029
his parents' death in the fire that the headlines
have changed.

00:14:22.029 --> 00:14:26.649
Originally, the headline emphasised that Mike's
parents were drug addicts putting blame on

00:14:26.649 --> 00:14:29.860
the victims rather than the perpetrators of
the atrocity.

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:34.579
After IT's death though, the headline has
changed to a more neutral report of two locals

00:14:34.579 --> 00:14:36.370
dying in a house fire.

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:40.920
By destroying the evil beneath, it's as if
the monster's malignant influence on the town

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:42.440
is disappearing.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:47.120
What's more, this time even after the Losers
leave Derry, they no longer forget what happened

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:48.960
and their memories remain intact.

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:53.329
When Mike talks to Bill on the phone, he wonders
if it's just because IT is dead, or if it's

00:14:53.329 --> 00:14:56.990
because they now have more they want to remember
than forget.

00:14:56.990 --> 00:15:01.690
Before the film ends we also discover that
Stanley wrote a letter to the Losers before

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:03.100
taking his own life.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:07.420
The letter explains how Stan believed that
what he did gave the Losers the best chance

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:11.449
against IT as he knew he was too terrified
to go back to Derry.

00:15:11.449 --> 00:15:16.050
Stan tried to repress his memories of Pennywise
in his life, but when Mike calls, Stan tries

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:20.650
to push back with questions hoping to buy
time, but it seems like he was always expecting

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:23.910
this moment and he simply says, "It's come
back, hasn't it?"

00:15:23.910 --> 00:15:28.530
Although all the Losers were terrorised by
Pennywise as kids that summer, Stan perhaps

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:33.000
suffered the worst when he was almost eaten
alive after IT separated him from the rest

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:35.050
of the group in the sewers.

00:15:35.050 --> 00:15:40.079
Pennywise had his huge razor-sharp jaws wrapped
around Stan's face and for him that memory

00:15:40.079 --> 00:15:43.730
was just too terrifying and he couldn't face
IT again.

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:47.600
Always the most rational member of the group,
in his letter, Stan explains that he made

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:51.720
what he saw as the most logical move, and
took himself off the board.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:56.160
By bringing the number of Losers alive down
from seven to six, in his view they could

00:15:56.160 --> 00:16:00.230
remain united, which they wouldn't have done
if he'd lived but hadn't returned to Derry.

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:05.380
In this version of the story, Stan is somewhat
redeemed as we hear him say the words "I swear,

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:09.600
Bill" in his final moments, which in a way
meant he fulfilled the promise he made at

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:10.910
the blood oath.

00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:15.759
An additional Chapter Two scene of young Stan
giving his Bar Mitzvah speech also stops adult

00:16:15.759 --> 00:16:20.079
Richie from abandoning the Losers, and Richie
thanks Stan for showing up for him in his

00:16:20.079 --> 00:16:21.579
time of need.

00:16:21.579 --> 00:16:25.340
Stan also acknowledges in the letter that's
he's lived his whole life being afraid and

00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:30.069
encourages everyone else not to be this way
and instead be proud of who they are and who

00:16:30.069 --> 00:16:31.279
they want to be.

00:16:31.279 --> 00:16:36.860
This last point seems especially pertinent
to Richie who we see re-carving R+E on the

00:16:36.860 --> 00:16:41.279
bridge, an indication that after Eddie's death,
he'll no longer hide his sexuality.

00:16:41.279 --> 00:16:44.760
But the point also relates to the other Losers.

00:16:44.760 --> 00:16:48.880
Mike finally decides to leave Derry for a
new life, and Bev and Ben are now together

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:53.589
in a happy, healthy relationship, with Bev's
endless nightmares replaced with beautiful

00:16:53.589 --> 00:16:54.589
dreams.

00:16:54.589 --> 00:16:58.750
For Bill, defeating IT for good means he's
been able to move on from the ending of that

00:16:58.750 --> 00:17:02.819
screenplay he couldn't finish, and he's now
actually writing the first chapter/beginning

00:17:02.819 --> 00:17:04.069
of a new story.

00:17:04.069 --> 00:17:08.780
In fact, that story we see on screen is a
passage from Stephen King's novel IT.

